schema: "0.4"
id: npl-ux-d4-topbar-bento-home-bento
type: image
quality: high

# Direction D4: top-bar only + bento home — screen: org home as a bento grid of section tiles
# Nocturne palette (exact hexes, dark-native canvas — never pure #000/#fff): canvas #010409, panel #0d1117, raised #161b22, border #21262d, primary text #e6edf3 (soft off-white ink), secondary text #909dab, muted text #6e7681, signal green (live/primary accent) #3fb950, link cyan (navigation) #58a6ff, amber (rare warning) #d29922, error coral #f85149. Type: Inter for UI/labels, JetBrains Mono (co-equal voice) for counts, timestamps, ids, code, SQL, paths. Shape: flat surfaces separated by lightness steps only, 4px radius, no drop shadows, no glow, no gradients, no neon bloom, no OLED pitch-black, no pure-white surfaces.

prompt:
  system: |
    You are a senior product designer rendering a high-fidelity dark-native app UI
    for NoizuPromptLingo. This direction has NO SIDEBAR AT ALL: navigation lives
    entirely in a persistent TOP BAR (org switcher, primary destinations as
    horizontal tabs/links, search, notifications, user menu). Section landing
    pages and the home screen are BENTO grids of tiles. Render as a real product
    screenshot, never a wireframe.
  text: |
        A 16:9 high-fidelity UI mockup of NoizuPromptLingo's org Home screen,
        testing the TOP-BAR-ONLY + BENTO shell direction — NO left sidebar of
        any kind.

        TOP BAR (full width, panel tone #0d1117, persistent, no sidebar below
        it anywhere): far left an org switcher ("Acme Robotics ▾") next to a
        small wordmark "NPL"; center-left a horizontal row of EXACTLY EIGHT
        primary destination LINKS as text (not icons), in this EXACT order
        and with this EXACT spelling — no synonyms, no rewording, no
        additional or substitute labels: "Home", "Work", "Chat", "Knowledge",
        "Files", "Data", "Integrations", "Settings". "Home" is the active
        item (green underline). The eight labels must be spelled exactly as
        listed; no other nav labels. Far right: a search affordance
        ("/ search") with a visible "/" keyboard-shortcut hint, a
        notification bell with a green unread badge "5", and a user avatar.

        BELOW THE TOP BAR, full-width BENTO GRID (the entire home screen is this
        grid, no side rails): an uneven mosaic of tiles on raised tone (#161b22),
        4px radius, flat, hairline borders only. A large hero tile "Continue
        where you left off" showing a session card ("sess-7f21 — Refactor auth
        middleware", mono duration "running · 14m"). A medium tile "Work" with
        mono stat rows ("27 open tickets", "6 boards"). A medium tile "Chat"
        showing 2 recent room previews with unread green dots. A tall tile
        "Notifications" listing 4 compact inbox rows with mono timestamps. A
        small tile "Files" showing a mount name and a green "connected" pill. A
        small tile "Data" showing a tenant scope chip and a mini sparkline-style
        row of mono query-count numbers. A wide bottom tile "First-run
        checklist" with 4 checklist rows, 2 checked in green.

        Use realistic, specific product content throughout — never lorem ipsum.

  negative: "watermark, signature, lorem ipsum placeholder text, low-fidelity wireframe, monitor/device photograph framing, blurry, distorted UI, neon glow, bloom, CRT scanlines, gradient background, pure-black OLED background, pure-white surfaces, warm amber/gold dominant palette, light-mode canvas"

attachments:
  - path: _nocturne-palette.png
    role: reference
    description: "Locked Nocturne palette swatches (bg, surface, border, text, muted, accent, success, danger) with hex labels — match these exact colors, do not reinterpret."

output:
  formats:
    - format: png
  dimensions:
    width: 1920
    height: 1080
    aspect_ratio: "16:9"

service: gemini
provider_options:
  generate_content_model: gemini-2.5-flash-image

eval:
  pass_threshold: 0.72
  criteria:
    relevance: {weight: 3, description: "Shows a full-width persistent top bar with org switcher, and exactly the eight horizontal text destination links Home, Work, Chat, Knowledge, Files, Data, Integrations, Settings in that exact order and spelling (Home active), search, notifications, and user menu, with NO sidebar anywhere, and a full-width uneven bento grid of home tiles (continue-session hero, work stats, chat, notifications, files, data, checklist)"}
    consistent_top_bar: {weight: 2, description: "Top bar nav labels exactly match the eight specified labels and order, identical in structure to the paired settings-keys shot"}
    theme_fidelity: {weight: 3, description: "Dark-native Nocturne canvas (#010409/#0d1117), single phosphor-green #3fb950 signal, link cyan #58a6ff, amber #d29922 used sparingly, mono-first counts/timestamps/ids in JetBrains Mono, 4px radius, flat surface-step elevation, no shadow/glow/gradient"}
    composition: {weight: 2, description: "Top bar reads clearly as the only navigation chrome, bento tiles vary in size and form a legible mosaic, hero tile is visually dominant"}
    technical: {weight: 2, description: "Sharp, correct 16:9 aspect, no artifacts"}
  reject_if:
    - "lorem ipsum or placeholder text visible"
    - "watermark or signature visible"
    - "wireframe-level fidelity instead of high-fidelity mockup"
    - "neon glow, bloom, or gradient wash"
    - "light-mode or warm/gold dominant canvas instead of dark-native Nocturne"
    - "nav labels differ from the eight specified"

tags: [ux-overhaul, npl-nocturne, NoizuPromptLingo, shell-direction, direction-4]
